$DIR/main.p:7:12: invalid argument: take needs a pointer to the place to take from, not x (variable of type int)
    take moves a value out of a place, a field, an element or a variable reached
    through a pointer, and leaves the zero value there. It takes the place's
    address, so that it can write the zero value back.
    Pass the address of the place:
        v := take(&x.field)
    (see "Moving out of a place" in the Plutonium spec, section 13.10)
    (run "pluto explain E3208" for a longer explanation)
